  "reason": "The current best is config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.619 accuracy. The image-only baseline (0.208) is very weak, suggesting the image branch contributes limited signal. The key uncertainty is whether the concat fusion in config_018 is optimal or whether weighted fusion could better balance the strong RNA signal (0.591) with the weak image signal. Config_019 changes only the fusion method (concat → weighted) while keeping all other settings identical to config_018, providing a clean A/B comparison. This is the best use of experiment 7 because it is a minimal, single-variable test of the most immediate improvement lever on the current best configuration. If weighted fusion wins, we have a clear new best; if not, we eliminate that direction and can focus remaining budget on the image encoder (e.g., ViT-L) or other dimensions."
}

